    "lastCommit": {
      "id": "ed7995107da8fe1f5b513cd307b593768334ec55",
      "message": "[ota-hal] OTA-1738 \u2014 the game teaches what it runs (task list 4E91C7)\n\nPlayer-teaching repair pass under the eleven locked owner decisions. No\nmechanic, price, yield, cap or balance rule is touched; every teaching\nsurface now describes the rule the engine actually runs, and no two\noptional cards can land on one beat.\n\nCopy, in one place\n- app/components/teachingRegistry.ts holds every first-use card (id,\n  title, body, group, trigger line). Rules are quoted from the constants\n  that run them: REINFORCE_MAX_LEVEL, REPLACEMENT_DOG_PRICE /\n  FACTION_DOG_PRICE, scrapSuccessChance, COATING_DOT_TURNS,\n  LOYALTY_DECAY_HOURS + DOG_LOYALTY_BANDS (new, dogCompanion),\n  STAMINA_COSTS.wander (moved to app/engine/staminaCosts.ts, re-exported by\n  the store), PITY_KILL_INTERVAL (app/engine/resurrectionRules.ts).\n- Cards whose rule changed carry new ids: torch_first_v2 (each USE spends\n  one torch \u2014 not a lamp burning while lit), golem_first_v2 (fed its own\n  parts, or a trader; kits do not heal it), combat_throw_spear_v2 (one\n  spear spent on every concluded throw, hit or miss), contracts_first_open_v3\n  (a hunt's trophy is shown in person), crafting_tab_repair_v2 (MATERIALS at\n  the bench; the trader mends for TC).\n- New cards: reinforce_first, workings_first, repair_vendor_first,\n  dog_replacement_first, scrap_first, throwables_first, race_ability_first.\n\nThe first fight\n- The primer is once per INSTALL through useFirstTimeHint (combat_primer_v1):\n  the global tips switch and SHOW ALL TIPS AGAIN govern it; closing it still\n  latches the per-save milestone. The kill-count gate is gone.\n- POWER is taught in the primer (the power_number card is retired); the\n  readout card waits for the fight after the first, once the primer is seen.\n- FLEE row quotes FLEE_STAMINA_COST and states the failure half; DODGE\n  quotes DODGE_COOLDOWN_ROUNDS; STEALTH is rewritten to the handler: before\n  contact a passed roll is a free opening (no volley, +5, once per scene),\n  once engaged a contest they answer either way.\n\nOne optional surface per beat\n- useTeachingSlot (useFirstTimeHint.ts) picks the ONE unseen, eligible\n  card from a fixed candidate list; presentation order only, each `when` is\n  the control's own predicate. ExplorationScreen renders a single\n  FirstTimeHint from it; the primer, the mission stinger and the beat card\n  defer every candidate. Inventory and Vendor screens do the same.\n- climb_first waits for the tutorial to end; torch_first_v2 keys on the\n  charged lead; THROW SPEAR keys on spareThrowingSpear (new in\n  bandolierEligibility, shared with InputBox).\n\nThe outpost and the replay\n- Door beat carries one movement-cost sentence; the close names Ask the\n  Arbiter once. TutorialOverlay asks isTutorialLocked, so SKIP is offered\n  on look / armor / screen_pick too.\n- Settings \u2192 GUIDANCE \u2192 REPLAY TEACHING opens GuidanceScreen ('guidance'\n  route): CORE (outpost beats + the corrected screen tour: pity 100, no\n  first-install gem, no MAP button, no ACTIONS screen), FIRST-USE (every\n  card, grouped, \u2713 seen \u2014 read-only), REFERENCE (ActionReferenceBody, the\n  Action Reference reachable at last).\n- Dog onboarding teaches feeding, the decay clock and the permanent walk.\n- The bounty primer obeys the tips switch and the reset (install flag via\n  isHintSeen / markHintSeen; bountyPrimerSeen still written).\n\nTests\n- New: ota1738TheGameTeachesWhatItRuns (runtime-proven stealth opener,\n  spear spend on hit and miss, torch spend, scrap failure yield, tile-step\n  cost, dog decay, bounty primer under switch/reset; registry ids; source\n  structure of the slot) and ota1738TheReplayAndTheSlot (teaching slot,\n  primer \"turn off tips\", GuidanceScreen read-only with tips off, SKIP pill\n  on every locked beat).\n- Nine pin suites re-anchored to the registry and the slot (1163, 1205,\n  1245, 1249, 1321, 1511, 1523, 1524, 1531).\n\nReported, not fixed: the typed verb \"stealth\" parses as `steal` (\"Nothing\nto steal here\"); the STEALTH button submits `sneak`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LGFtzR6AQJbu4XdR28y3fX",
      "dateCreated": "2026-09-07T17:07:17Z",
